# Route conventions

Routes live in `src/routes/<domain>.routes.ts`. They wire middleware chains and nothing else.

## Canonical middleware chain

```typescript
router.get(
  '/:id',
  optionalAuthenticate,                                  // 1. auth guard (optional or required)
  validate(idSchema, ValidationType.PARAMS),             // 2. param validation
  isEventOrganizerOrAdmin,                               // 3. authorization (after auth, before handler)
  validate(querySchema, ValidationType.QUERY),           // 4. query/body validation
  asyncHandler(getById)                                  // 5. handler — always last, always asyncHandler
);
```

## Import pattern

```typescript
import { Router } from 'express';
import { asyncHandler } from '../utils/asyncHandler';
import { authenticate, optionalAuthenticate } from '../middleware/auth.middleware';
import { isEventOrganizerOrAdmin } from '../middleware/authorization.middleware';
import { requireAdmin } from '../middleware/admin.middleware';
import { validate, ValidationType } from '../middleware/validation.middleware';
import { <domain>IdSchema, create<Domain>Schema } from '../validators/<domain>.validator';
import { get<Domain>s, create<Domain> } from '../controllers/<domain>.controller';

const router = Router();
// ... routes ...
export default router;
```

## Auth guard selection

| Route type | Guard |
|---|---|
| Public (no user needed) | no auth middleware |
| Attaches user if present, no rejection | `optionalAuthenticate` |
| Requires valid token, 401 if missing | `authenticate` |
| Requires admin role | `authenticate` + `requireAdmin` |
| Requires organizer or admin | `authenticate` + `isEventOrganizerOrAdmin` |

## Static vs dynamic paths

Named static paths (e.g., `/my`, `/single`, `/count`) **must come before** `/:id` in the file, otherwise Express matches them as IDs:

```typescript
router.get('/my', authenticate, asyncHandler(getMyItems));     // ✓ before /:id
router.get('/:id', optionalAuthenticate, asyncHandler(getById)); // ✓ after
```

## Route registration in `src/app.ts`

After creating a new route file, register it in `src/app.ts`:
```typescript
import <domain>Routes from './routes/<domain>.routes';
app.use('/api/<domain>s', apiLimiter, <domain>Routes);
```

Always pass `apiLimiter`. Use `authLimiter` (stricter) only for auth routes.

## Do not

- Add business logic in route files
- Call handlers without `asyncHandler` — uncaught async errors crash Express 5
- Forget to register new route files in `src/app.ts`
